<worksheet >
    <title>APP-1 Line Integrals and Vector Fields</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, you will need to correctly complete all three problems. 
      To earn a P on this outcome, you will need to correctly complete problem 1 and 1 part 
      of problems 2 and 3 with progress on the other parts.</p>
  </introduction>  
  <page>
    <exercise workspace="2.5in"><p>Evaluate <m>\int_C(x^3y)dS</m> where 
      <m>C</m> is the upper half of the circle <m>x^2 + y^2 = 1</m>.</p></exercise>
  </page>
  <page>
    <exercise>
        <introduction><p>Let <m>\vec{F}(x,y)=\langle y, -x+1 \rangle</m>.</p></introduction>
        <task workspace="2.0in"><statement><p>Give a sketch of the vector field for the integer points in <m>[-1,1]\times[-1,1]</m></p></statement></task>
        <task workspace="2.0in"><statement><p>Assume that <m>\vec{F}</m> represents a velocity field and the position 
          of a particle in the field at time <m>t=4</m> is <m>(5,-2)</m>.  Estimate the location of the particle 
          at time <m>t=4.01</m>.</p></statement></task>
    </exercise>
    </page>
    <page>
    <exercise>
        <introduction><p> Given <m>\vec{F}(x,y)=\langle 2xy^3+5e^{5x},3x^2y^2+\sec^2{y} \rangle</m> for <m>y \gt 0</m>.</p></introduction>
        <task workspace="2.0in"><statement><p>Show that <m>\vec{F}</m> is conservative.</p></statement></task>
        <task workspace="2.0in"><statement><p>Find the potential function if it exists. If it does not exist, explain why.</p></statement></task>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>